Subject: [PATCH 6/7] media: qcom: camss: csiphy: let a CSIPHY feed several CSIDs

A CSID demultiplexes four streams at most (three RDIs on a full one), and a
D4XX camera has seven: four images and the embedded metadata of three of
them, each a (virtual channel, data type) of its own. On this generation of
the CSID a path captures exactly one data type - the register that adds a
second VC/DT to a path only exists from Titan 480 on - so the seven streams
need seven paths.

Allow more than one enabled link from a CSIPHY source pad, so that a lite
CSID (four RDIs) and a full one (three) can both receive from the camera's
CSIPHY. Each CSID selects its PHY input on its own, which is how the vendor
driver runs two CSIDs on one sensor for dual-IFE. The CSIPHY already counts
its streams across every CSID, and the sensor is started stream by stream.

A CSIPHY with a clock mux that names a single CSID keeps the one-link rule.
---
--- a/camss-csiphy.c
+++ b/camss-csiphy.c
@@ -790,12 +790,18 @@ static int csiphy_link_setup(struct medi
 		struct csiphy_device *csiphy;
 		struct csid_device *csid;
 
-		if (media_pad_remote_pad_first(local))
-			return -EBUSY;
-
 		sd = media_entity_to_v4l2_subdev(entity);
 		csiphy = v4l2_get_subdevdata(sd);
 
+		/*
+		 * A CSID demultiplexes four streams at most, so a sensor with
+		 * more needs several CSIDs on its CSIPHY, each taking its own
+		 * share. Only a CSIPHY whose clock mux names one CSID is held
+		 * to a single link.
+		 */
+		if (csiphy->base_clk_mux && media_pad_remote_pad_first(local))
+			return -EBUSY;
+
 		sd = media_entity_to_v4l2_subdev(remote->entity);
 		csid = v4l2_get_subdevdata(sd);
 
